# GMS throws three blue flames, each splitting once as it lands, up to eleven
# in all. Every flame burns ONE enemy for 380% four times and leaves it burning
# for half a minute; a flame landing on an enemy another already reached keeps
# 45% of its final damage. All GMS's own numbers.
#
# Scatter is what carries that -- see Skill.scatter. It matters most where the
# skill does: against a lone boss all eleven flames land on it, worth five and
# a half swings, where an ordinary eleven-enemy reading would land one.
#
# GMS sends the flames at bosses first, highest HP first. The fight spends the
# leftover flames on the healthiest, which is the same rule read through a game
# whose queue holds no bosses.
#
# The delay is ours: GMS states none, and 660ms is what every other cast in
# this book takes.
name: "Megiddo Flame"
description:
  "Fires a blue flame that burns the enemy to the very soul. After burning an "
  "enemy, the blue flame spreads to a set number of additional targets."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
tags: SKILL_TAG_FIRE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_ARCH_MAGE skill_order: 2 }
hyper: true
required_level: 160
max_level: 1
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_STAFF
base_delay_ms: 660
max_enemies: 11
lines: 4
cooldown_seconds: 50.0
base { skill_pct: 3.80 }
scatter {
  hits: 11
  repeat_final_dmg_pct: -0.55
}
dot {
  interval_seconds: 1.0
  duration_seconds: 30.0
  lines: 1
  base { skill_pct: 7.00 }
}
